# Copy to apps/mobile/.env (gitignored). Restart Metro / rebuild JS after changing.
# Do not use Expo Go. Native BLE requires a development client (`expo-dev-client`).
# This file has no secrets — only the public API origin.
#
# Metro / USB development client should target the **local** API (not Fly).
# EAS `production` and cloud `development` profiles stay on hop-uokqmg — do not
# change eas.json for laptop Postgres work. Metro JS inlines this file at bundle time.

# Simulator / this Mac:
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Physical iPhone talking to a Mac LAN API (required for 7-tap rate-limit reset).
# Localhost on the phone is the phone itself and cannot reach your Mac.
# Find the Mac LAN IP:  ipconfig getifaddr en0
# Then set (this machine's Wi-Fi example):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.170:8000
#
# The API must bind all interfaces:  ./scripts/run_dev.sh  or
#   uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
# Development builds allow cleartext HTTP only to loopback and RFC1918 LAN IPs.
# iOS ATS local-networking is enabled for that LAN HTTP path.
# Release builds refuse LAN cleartext — production must stay HTTPS.
#
# Live Fly (only if you intentionally leave Metro on production):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://hop-uokqmg.fly.dev
# The in-app banner shows PRODUCTION when the URL host is hop-uokqmg.fly.dev
# (and when GET /version env=production). Local/LAN shows DEV.

# Android emulator (host machine from the AVD):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
